p2u: 1
deck:
  title: Present2u
  subtitle: Technical presentations, beautifully made
  theme: writebook
  meta:
    product: Present2u
slides:
  - layout: title
    title: Present2u
    subtitle: Technical presentations, beautifully made

  - layout: content
    title: Author in the Format You Want
    body: |
      Write slides in **Markdown** with `$math$`, or drop into **Typst** for
      full typesetting control — both are first-class.

      - Markdown: fast, familiar, great for prose and code
      - Typst: precise layout, native math, one file per slide
      - Switch per deck with a single field

  - layout: content
    title: Diagrams and Math, Rendered for You
    body: |
      Diagrams and equations are compiled server-side and embedded as crisp
      SVG, so they look right on any screen.

      - **D2** diagrams, including the hand-drawn sketch style
      - **LaTeX** equations via pdflatex, or **Typst** math
      - Inline `$...$` rendered with KaTeX in the browser

  - layout: diagram
    title: One Deck, Many Engines
    blocks:
      - kind: diagram
        lang: d2-sketch
        source: |
          direction: right
          author: Author
          present2u: "Present2u"
          out: "Deck"
          author -> present2u: "Markdown / Typst"
          present2u -> out: "SVG + HTML"
          out -> author: "Present / Export"

  - layout: content
    title: Present and Share
    body: |
      Everything you build can be presented live or exported as a single file.

      - Fullscreen 16:9 presenting with notes and an overview
      - Export a self-contained HTML deck, or print to PDF
      - Long slides scroll instead of being clipped

  - layout: recap
    title: Get Started
    body: |
      - Start from a template or a blank deck
      - Write Markdown or Typst — your choice
      - Add D2 diagrams and LaTeX or Typst math
      - Present it, or export and share it